---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Zarlino Audio"
  description="How Zarlino Audio collects, uses, and protects your information."
  canonicalURL="https://zarlinoaudio.com/legal/privacy"
  schemaType="website"
>
  <main class="relative z-[1] bg-[#050505] min-h-screen pt-24 pb-24 px-6 md:px-10">
    <div class="max-w-[820px] mx-auto">
      <nav class="mb-8 font-['Inter'] text-[13px] text-[#64748B]">
        <a href="/" class="hover:text-white transition-colors">Zarlino Audio</a>
        <span class="mx-2">/</span>
        <span class="text-[#94A3B8]">Privacy Policy</span>
      </nav>

      <h1 class="font-['Space_Grotesk'] font-semibold text-white text-[clamp(32px,4.5vw,48px)] leading-[1.1] tracking-[-0.02em]">
        Privacy Policy
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-3 font-['IBM_Plex_Mono'] text-[12px] uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-[#64748B]">
        Version 1.0 · 2 October 2026
      </p>

      <div class="mt-10 font-['Inter'] text-[16px] text-[#94A3B8] leading-[1.8] space-y-8">
        <p>
          This policy explains what information Zarlino Audio ("we", "us") collects when you use
          zarlinoaudio.com, buy or license our software, or contact us — and what we do with it.
        </p>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-['Space_Grotesk'] font-semibold text-white text-[22px] mb-3">1. Who we are</h2>
          <p>
            Zarlino Audio (Ghana) develops and sells audio software. You can reach us at
            <a href="mailto:support@zarlinoaudio.com" class="text-[#00D4FF] hover:underline">support@zarlinoaudio.com</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-['Space_Grotesk'] font-semibold text-white text-[22px] mb-3">2. What we collect</h2>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
            <li><strong class="text-[#CBD5E1]">Purchase details</strong> — the email address you enter at checkout and the items you bought. Card and payment details are handled by Paystack; we never see or store your card number.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-[#CBD5E1]">Licence keys</strong> — the key issued to your email address, kept so we can re-issue it if you lose it.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-[#CBD5E1]">Updates list</strong> — the email address you give when you ask to be notified about releases.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-[#CBD5E1]">Feedback you send</strong> — bug reports and suggestions, including any email address you include. Bug reports are handled through a public issue tracker, so please don't include personal information you don't want to be public.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-[#CBD5E1]">Technical data</strong> — basic request logs from our hosting provider (for example IP address and timestamps) used for security and aggregate visit counting.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-['Space_Grotesk'] font-semibold text-white text-[22px] mb-3">3. How we use it</h2>
          <p>
            To deliver your purchase and licence, provide support and re-issue keys, send the release
            updates you asked for, keep the store secure and prevent abuse, and meet our legal and
            accounting obligations. We use automated systems to help run the store and support
            workflows; these are reviewed by us.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-['Space_Grotesk'] font-semibold text-white text-[22px] mb-3">4. Who we share it with</h2>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
            <li><strong class="text-[#CBD5E1]">Cloudflare</strong> — hosting and storage for this website and our internal systems.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-[#CBD5E1]">Paystack</strong> — payment processing; their own privacy policy applies to payment data.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-[#CBD5E1]">GitHub</strong> — public bug reports and suggestions you submit may appear as public issues.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-2">We do not sell your personal information.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-['Space_Grotesk'] font-semibold text-white text-[22px] mb-3">5. Retention &amp; your rights</h2>
          <p>
            We keep purchase and licence records for as long as needed to deliver licences and meet
            legal obligations; update-list addresses until you unsubscribe. You can ask us to access,
            correct, or delete your personal information, or to stop using it for updates, by emailing
            <a href="mailto:support@zarlinoaudio.com" class="text-[#00D4FF] hover:underline">support@zarlinoaudio.com</a>.
            Nothing in this policy limits rights you have under applicable data-protection law.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-['Space_Grotesk'] font-semibold text-white text-[22px] mb-3">6. Changes</h2>
          <p>If this policy changes materially we will update this page and the version date above.</p>
        </section>

        <p class="pt-4 border-t border-[rgba(255,255,255,0.06)] text-[13px] text-[#475569]">
          Plain-language version 1.0 — pending legal review. We will publish an updated version once reviewed.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
